model.en:
// h2 with transparent h1 fallback
const srv = http2.createSecureServer({ key, cert: fullchain, allowHTTP1: true }); srv.on('stream', (stream, headers) => { stream.respond({ ':status': 200 }); stream.end('h2'); }); srv.on('request', (req, res) => { res.end('h1'); }); // fires only for ALPN 'http/1.1'
ALPN is an extension to the TLS ClientHello: the client advertises ['h2','http/1.1'], the server picks one, and the chosen protocol is known the instant the handshake completes — zero extra latency. allowHTTP1 makes the same listener answer old clients without a second port.

